      "document_classification": "AI_ONLY",
      "inputText": "I need a moment to celebrate, because after years of work my novel is finally finished. And I don't just mean a rough draft. I mean rewrites, revisions, painful cuts, and more passes than I can count. There were long stretches where I genuinely believed I'd never reach the end, where the manuscript felt like a problem I'd never solve. But here I am. What surprised me most is how anticlimactic the final moment felt, just a quiet sense of completion rather than fireworks. The real reward was all the small breakthroughs along the way, the scenes that suddenly clicked after the tenth attempt. I'm sharing this partly to mark the occasion and partly to encourage anyone in the middle of a long project: the slog is real, but persistence genuinely pays off. If you're deep in revisions and doubting yourself, please keep going. Thank you all for being a community that makes this lonely work feel a little less lonely.\n",
